<title>JAPAN: Banyu says gets approval to import Merck HIV drug.</title>
<headline>Banyu says gets approval to import Merck HIV drug.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banyu Pharmaceutical Co Ltd said on Monday it has received approval from Japan's Health Ministry to import an HIV drug developed by Merck and Co Inc of the United States.  </p>
<p>Banyu will start marketing the drug, Crixivan, in Japan on April 1, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The drug, approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration in March 1996, is approved in 49 countries, including Japan, the statement said. The drug is currently being prescribed to 135,000 HIV patients worldwide, it said.</p>
